# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC AND MUST STAY GENERIC AND ANONYMOUS.
#
# MUSAI is run against a live university Moodle with real courses, real
# colleagues and real students. That operational material is what makes the
# project work and it is exactly what must never be published, so the split is
# structural rather than editorial:
#
#   PUBLIC  — the engine: `musai/`, `tests/`, `alembic/`, this file, README.
#   PRIVATE — everything that names a person, a live course or a credential:
#             the working notes, the operational scripts, the data they harvest.
#
# Nothing below is deleted from your working copy. These files stay on disk as
# the local record; they simply never enter the history.
#
# ⭐ The rule that produced this file: EXCLUDE THE SURFACE, DON'T REDACT IT.
# An allow-list of "safe" outputs is only ever as current as the last person who
# remembered to update it — an audit on 2026-08-16 found two probe dumps sitting
# in the history with twelve students' full names and matrículas in them,
# un-ignored by an explicit `!` exception whose comment claimed they contained
# "no person". Redaction fails quietly and permanently. Exclusion does not.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env
!.env.example
# Google OAuth client download. The app reads .env, never this file.
client_secret_*.json

# ── Working notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The session log, the per-course worksheets, the runbooks and the product
# notes. These are the most valuable documents in the project and the least
# publishable: they name colleagues, quote them, record which of their courses
# were written to and when, and carry live course identifiers throughout.
# Every Markdown file is private by default; the public README is the exception.
*.md
!README.md

# ── Operational scripts and everything they harvest ──────────────────────────
# One-shot drivers and probes written against live courses: they carry course
# ids, professor usernames and group codes in their names alone, and they write
# rosters, message logs, quiz answer keys and pre-delete dumps beside
# themselves. The directory is excluded whole — no allow-list, no exceptions.
scratchpad/

# ── Student and course data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Moodle backups carry enrolments, submissions and grades inside the .mbz.
course_backups/
*.mbz
# Archives uploaded through the cockpit — same content, arriving from the other
# direction, and one per professor, so a colleague's course data lands here too.
uploads/
# The dev DB holds real rosters, matrículas and partial grades.
musai_dev.db
musai_dev.db.bak-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Per-run rollback records and section snapshots — the local undo trail.
backups/

# ── Copyrighted material ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Textbook scans used to author course content.
resources/
*.jpeg
*.jpg

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Playwright / runtime artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
screenshots/
*.png
downloads/
*.csv
*.ods
*.xlsx

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
